ad the worked example and complete independent tasks.","passage":"532−268","prompts":["What facts or numbers are given?","What method do I need?","Show my answer.","Verify my answer."]},"reflection_prompts":null,"reflection_prompt":null,"teach_steps":[{"icon":"🔎","title":"Align hundreds, tens and ones","explain":"**Topic-specific teaching:** 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds.\n\n**Focus on this idea:** Align hundreds, tens and ones. Work from the original facts in 532−268.","example":"**Worked example:** 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds.\n\n**Guided attempt:** Check 532−268 using the written or mental method. The result is 264.\n\n**Now independently try:** The school has 703 chairs and moves 458 outside. Calculate 703−458, then 615−278. Show exchanges across the zero and check both answers.","notice":"Check the relevant values and evidence; align hundreds, tens and ones is not a guessing activity.","check":{"question":"What is 532−268?","options":["254","264","274","364"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"264 is correct. 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds."},"visual_before":[{"episode":{"title":"A clue about Written Subtraction: Regroup and Verify","transcript":"Pip: I''m studying written subtraction: regroup and verify. How do I know which method to use?\nJuno: Read the example and identify the important numbers or exact words before answering.\nPip: Then I can compare my work with a second method or source to check it.\nJuno: Yes. Pause now and explain one useful check in your own words. The evidence matters more than a quick guess.","scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"who":"pip","text":"I''m studying written subtraction: regroup and verify. How do I know which method to use?"},{"who":"juno","text":"Read the example and identify the important numbers or exact words before answering."},{"who":"pip","text":"Then I can compare my work with a second method or source to check it."},{"who":"juno","text":"Yes. Pause now and explain one useful check in your own words. The evidence matters more than a quick guess.","pause_after":true}]}]}}]},{"icon":"🧠","title":"Exchange one ten for ten ones","explain":"**Topic-specific teaching:** 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds.\n\n**Focus on this idea:** Exchange one ten for ten ones. Work from the original facts in 532−268.","example":"**Worked example:** 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds.\n\n**Guided attempt:** Check 421−176 using the written or mental method. The result is 245.\n\n**Now independently try:** The school has 703 chairs and moves 458 outside. Calculate 703−458, then 615−278. Show exchanges across the zero and check both answers.","notice":"Check the relevant values and evidence; exchange one ten for ten ones is not a guessing activity.","check":{"question":"What is 421−176?","options":["235","245","255","345"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"245 is correct. 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds."}},{"icon":"✏️","title":"Exchange one hundred for ten tens","explain":"**Topic-specific teaching:** 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds.\n\n**Focus on this idea:** Exchange one hundred for ten tens. Work from the original facts in 532−268.","example":"**Worked example:** 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds.\n\n**Guided attempt:** Check 604−257 using the written or mental method. The result is 347.\n\n**Now independently try:** The school has 703 chairs and moves 458 outside. Calculate 703−458, then 615−278. Show exchanges across the zero and check both answers.","notice":"Check the relevant values and evidence; exchange one hundred for ten tens is not a guessing activity.","check":{"question":"What is 604−257?","options":["337","347","357","447"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"347 is correct. 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds."}},{"icon":"✅","title":"Verify by inverse addition","explain":"**Topic-specific teaching:** 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds.\n\n**Focus on this idea:** Verify by inverse addition. Work from the original facts in 532−268.","example":"**Worked example:** 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds.\n\n**Guided attempt:** Check 703−458 using the written or mental method. The result is 245.\n\n**Now independently try:** The school has 703 chairs and moves 458 outside. Calculate 703−458, then 615−278. Show exchanges across the zero and check both answers.","notice":"Check the relevant values and evidence; verify by inverse addition is not a guessing activity.","check":{"question":"What is 703−458?","options":["235","245","255","345"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"245 is correct. 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds."}}],"worked_example":"Original situation: 532−268\n\n1. Align hundreds, tens and ones: 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds.\n\n2. Exchange one ten for ten ones: 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds.\n\n3. Exchange one hundred for ten tens: 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds.\n\n4. Verify by inverse addition: 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds.","worked_visuals":[{"svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 570 160\"><rect width=\"570\" height=\"160\" fill=\"#f0f6f1\"/><text x=\"15\" y=\"29\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-size=\"18\">Example: 532−268</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"55\" width=\"130\" height=\"85\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#dcefe4\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"94\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-size=\"12\">1. Align hundred</text><rect x=\"151\" y=\"55\" width=\"130\" height=\"85\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#e4eafa\"/><text x=\"157\" y=\"94\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-size=\"12\">2. Exchange one </text><rect x=\"292\" y=\"55\" width=\"130\" height=\"85\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#dcefe4\"/><text x=\"298\" y=\"94\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-size=\"12\">3. Exchange one </text><rect x=\"433\" y=\"55\" width=\"130\" height=\"85\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#e4eafa\"/><text x=\"439\" y=\"94\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-size=\"12\">4. Verify by inv</text></svg>","alt":"Four learning stages for Written Subtraction: Regroup and Verify","caption":"Use the full written worked example for the calculation or claim."}],"guided_practice":"**Read the model:** 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds.\n\n**Apply a similar step:** Start with 532−268, then explain which calculation or exchange gives 264.\n\n**Feedback:** 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds.","independent_task":"The school has 703 chairs and moves 458 outside. Calculate 703−458, then 615−278. Show exchanges across the zero and check both answers.","response_prompt":"The school has 703 chairs and moves 458 outside. Calculate 703−458, then 615−278. Show exchanges across the zero and check both answers.","quiz":[{"type":"multiple_choice","question":"What is 532−268?","options":["254","264","274","364"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"264 — 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds."},{"type":"multiple_choice","question":"What is 421−176?","options":["235","245","255","345"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"245 — 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds."},{"type":"multiple_choice","question":"What is 604−257?","options":["337","347","357","447"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"347 — 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds."},{"type":"multiple_choice","question":"What is 703−458?","options":["235","245","255","345"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"245 — 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds."},{"type":"multiple_choice","question":"What is 615−278?","options":["327","337","347","437"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"337 — 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds."},{"type":"multiple_choice","question":"What is 264+268?","options":["522","532","542","632"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"532 — 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds."},{"type":"multiple_choice","question":"What is 703−245?","options":["448","458","468","558"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"458 — 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds."},{"type":"multiple_choice","question":"What is 615−337?","options":["268","278","288","378"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"278 — 532−268=264. Regroup 532 as 4 hundreds, 12 tens and 12 ones. Subtract 8 ones, 6 tens and 2 hundreds."},{"type":"short_answer","question":"Complete the independent task with the required working and conclusions.","sample_answer":"703−458=245, because 703 regroups into 6 hundreds, 9 tens and 13 ones. Also 615−278=337.","marking_guide":"Check the original task against accurate calculation or text evidence.","explanation":"Explain the reasoning, not just the final answer."},{"type":"short_answer","question":"Explain a relevant correction, check or uncertainty in your reasoning.","sample_answer":"Checks: 245+458=703 and 337+278=615. A result of 355 for the first question fails because 355+458=813.","marking_guide":"Check the original task against accurate calculation or text evidence.","explanation":"Explain the reasoning, not just the final answer."}],"parent_notes":"Parent: Require an independent attempt before comparing answers.\n\nParent: Model 1: 703−458=245, because 703 regroups into 6 hundreds, 9 tens and 13 ones. Also 615−278=337.\n\nParent: Model 2: Checks: 245+458=703 and 337+278=615. A result of 355 for the first question fails because 355+458=813.\n\nParent: Check original work and confirm formal curriculum mapping separately.","evidence_instructions":"Save the independent task and written explanations.","offline_alternative":"Work with the complete original examples on paper and keep evidence.","extension":"Make another example of written subtraction: regroup and verify and verify it.","stage_hints":{"accept":["Review Written Subtraction: Regroup and Verify.","Identify a relevant original number or text detail.","Explain one reason your calculation or conclusion is correct."],"teach0":["Review Align hundreds, tens and ones.","Identify a relevant original number or text detail.","Explain one reason your calculation or conclusion is correct."],"teach1":["Review Exchange one ten for ten ones.","Identify a relevant original number or text detail.","Explain one reason your calculation or conclusion is correct."],"teach2":["Review Exchange one hundred for ten tens.","Identify a relevant original number or text detail.","Explain one reason your calculation or conclusion is correct."],"teach3":["Review Verify by inverse addition.","Identify a relevant original number or text detail.","Explain one reason your calculation or conclusion is correct."],"learn":["Review Written Subtraction: Regroup and Verify.","Identify a relevant original number or text detail.","Explain one reason your calculation or conclusion is correct."],"guided":["Review Written Subtraction: Regroup and Verify.","Identify a relevant original number or text detail.","Explain one reason your calculation or conclusion is correct."],"write":["Review Written Subtraction: Regroup and Verify.","Identify a relevant original number or text detail.","Explain one reason your calculation or conclusion is correct."],"quiz":["Review Written Subtraction: Regroup and Verify.","Identify a relevant original number or text detail.","Explain one reason your calculation or conclusion is correct."],"submit":["Review Written Subtraction: Regroup and Verify.","Identify a relevant original number or text detail.","Explain one reason your calculation or conclusion is correct."]}}') WHERE seed_key='s2-mat-y3-w07-l2';
